MVNO Graduation Demo — Audit & Real-Flow Hardening Run (2026-08-08)
===================================================================
Session: DeepSeek live-agent audit of "remove simulations -> real interactive flows".

The audit proposed removing product-logic simulations used as evidence. Investigation
empirically reframed the top blocker and hardened every flagged evidence step to REAL
behavior. All gates re-verified live.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. RTP BLOCKER RESOLVED (was a decode-artifact false alarm)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Handoff claimed the containerized baresip call produced "no RTP packets"
(`tshark -r <pcap> -Y rtp` = 0). Root cause: RTPEngine (drachtio mr9.4.0.0)
records pcap in `eth` format on ephemeral relay ports (e.g. UDP 30010-30050);
Wireshark's UDP->RTP heuristic does NOT auto-decode those ports, so -Y rtp reports
0 while the frames are 172-byte G.711 PCMU.

Forcing decode reveals media IS pinned through RTPEngine:
  - pcap 5aa83f5f… (early run): 703 RTP (caller->RTPEngine:30000) + 117 RTP (callee->30094)
  - pcap e4829224… (fresh run):  692 (caller->30050) + 195 (callee->30032)
  - tshark -d udp.port==30000,rtp yields RTP PT=ITU-T G.711 PCMU, so on
  - live_tap.sh --once uses data.data (not -Y rtp) and extracts per-leg WAVs fine.

Conclusion: media never stopped traversing RTPEngine; the demo now documents
that `-Y rtp` needs the decode directive and that live_tap is the extraction path.

