2. [5c] REAL CALL RECORDING -> WAV -> Vosk TRANSCRIPT (verified fresh)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
demo_call.sh setup+dial -> full baresip lifecycle through Kamailio:
  CALL_OUTGOING -> CALL_RINGING -> CALL_ANSWERED -> CALL_ESTABLISHED
  -> CALL_RTPESTAB(sendrecv) -> CALL_CLOSED ; rx answers = 1
Fresh pcap e4829224…: 192512 bytes. live_tap.sh --once -> callee leg 3.9s WAV,
caller leg 14.1s WAV. Vosk transcribed the callee leg of the LIVE call:
  { "text" : "you have won a prime target how are your account will be close" }

Hardening: demo_call.sh now renders the canned callee phrase longer
("You have won a prize, call us now or your account will be closed", 3.89 s)
so the [5c] WAV-duration >=3s floor holds on the speech-bearing callee leg;
the runbook [5c] now picks the NON-EMPTY leg (never the silent caller leg).

